Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: deb-pkg: use KBUILD_BUILD_TIMESTAMP for the changelog date

mkdebian writes the current time (`date -R`) into debian/changelog. The
linux-image .deb ships this file as changelog.Debian.gz, and its md5 goes
into the package's md5sums file. So the .deb and the installed package
change on every build, even when KBUILD_BUILD_TIMESTAMP is set. Also, if
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH is not set, dpkg-buildpackage takes it from this date.

When KBUILD_BUILD_TIMESTAMP is set, use it for the changelog date. Its value
is already a string that `date -d` accepts (Documentation/kbuild/kbuild.rst).
When it is not set, the date is the current time, as before.

Upstream mkdebian still uses `date -R` (v6.18 and master on 2026-11-21).
---
 scripts/package/mkdebian | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/package/mkdebian b/scripts/package/mkdebian
--- a/scripts/package/mkdebian
+++ b/scripts/package/mkdebian
@@ -197,7 +197,7 @@

   * Custom built Linux kernel.

- -- $maintainer  $(date -R)
+ -- $maintainer  $(date -R ${KBUILD_BUILD_TIMESTAMP:+-d "$KBUILD_BUILD_TIMESTAMP"})
 EOF

 # Generate a control file
